rds: `coding.md`, `ui-specification.md`, `definition-of-done-checklist.md`, `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Walk every spec §Phase (0 through 11) and assemble the spec coverage matrix. For each phase, locate the review file that covered it, capture the verdict, and propagate PASS / PASS-WITH-CAVEATS / BLOCK into this matrix. Any BLOCK from a prior review propagates to BLOCK here unless the blocking finding was resolved by a later follow-up task documented in this build.\n2. Walk every target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria → \"Initial targets\":\n   - 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks\n   - 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads\n   - 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks\n   - zero trusted display of known contradicted memory\n   - zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label\n   - 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks\n   For each, locate the evidence file (typically a benchmark report under `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/` or a test name under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/` or `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs`). Record evidence file path + value observed + target met/missed.\n3. Walk every risk from spec §Risks (Opaque Memory Mutation, Ranking Complexity, Event Log Growth, Stale Memory Leakage, Scope Leakage, Overfitting To Current Repo) and confirm the control documented in the spec is implemented and tested. For each, cite the implementation file and the test that proves the control.\n4. Run the full verification suite from a clean state:\n   - `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — full release build.\n   - `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace` — full daemon test workspace.\n   - `cd extension && npm run compile` — extension TypeScript compile.\n   - `cd extension && npm run lint` — extension lint.\n   - `cd extension && npm test` — extension test suite including R79's contract tests.\n   Any failure blocks the ship verdict.\n5. Confirm the deploy sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy works end-to-end: `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/`. Confirm the extension picks up the new binary.\n6. Confirm R88's `## Explicit Deferrals` section is either empty or every deferral meets the reason+owner+date bar; any silent deferral blocks the ship verdict per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n7. Confirm every spec §Non-Negotiable Product Property is satisfied (cross-reference with R83 workspace-boundary tests, R81 concurrency tests, R82 recovery tests, R87 hardening evidence).\n8. Confirm spec §Final Target is met: \"make a coding agent feel like it is operating in a workspace that remembers accurately.\" This is the qualitative final test — assemble evidence from R70 metrics + R78 frontend + R79 contract round-trips to argue the system delivers on each of the nine final-target bullet points.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real content, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec coverage matrix` — one row per spec §Phase (Phase 0 through Phase 11). Columns: phase, review file path, verdict (PASS / PASS-WITH-CAVEATS / BLOCK), notes (cite caveats by review-finding id if any).\n- `## Measurable success criteria` — one row per target from spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets (six targets). Columns: target text (verbatim from spec), evidence file path, value observed, met/missed verdict.\n- `## Risk controls in place` — one row per risk from spec §Risks (Opaque Memory Mutation, Ranking Complexity, Event Log Growth, Stale Memory Leakage, Scope Leakage, Overfitting To Current Repo). Columns: risk name, spec-mandated control, implementation file, test file/name that proves the control, verdict.\n- `## Ship verdict` — PASS or BLOCK. If PASS, the verdict line is a single declarative sentence: \"PASS — the cognitive-workspace fork ships.\" If BLOCK, the verdict line lists every blocker by id with a one-sentence summary, and the review opens a follow-up task in this build per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md` — confirms the review markdown exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec coverage matrix' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Measurable success criteria' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Risk controls in place' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `grep -q '## Ship verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R89-final-readiness.md`\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — release build succeeds.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace` — full daemon test workspace passes.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — extension compile succeeds.\n- `cd extension && npm run lint` — extension lint passes.\n- `cd extension && npm test` — extension test suite (including R79 contract tests) passes.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] All four mandatory sections present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] Every spec §Phase has a row in `## Spec coverage matrix` with a verdict.\n- [ ] Every spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target has a row in `## Measurable success criteria` with an evidence file path and a met/missed verdict.\n- [ ] Every spec §Risk has a row in `## Risk controls in place` with the implementation file and the test that proves the control.\n- [ ] Every verification command was actually executed from a clean checkout and the result captured.\n- [ ] `## Ship verdict` is either an unambiguous PASS or a BLOCK with named blockers.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, follow-up tasks are opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy — \"Never defer work you can do now\").\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
