_emitted_for_each_store_boundary_drop`; `hardening::workspace_boundary_tests::test_branch_and_session_scoped_memories_do_not_leak`; `…::test_repo_user_and_organization_scope_queries_require_explicit_opt_in`; `contract_tests::memory_verification_retrieval` (compile-time `&ScopeFilter` invariant audit). **All 7 + 6 + 6 green this review.** | **PASS.** |\n| **Overfitting To Current Repo** | \"fixture repos across languages, repo sizes, and documentation styles.\" | `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/fixtures/rust-repo/` (small, moderate-docs Rust service), `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/fixtures/typescript-repo/` (medium, rich-docs TS + React), `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/fixtures/python-repo/` (small, docstring-rich Python). `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/fixtures/README.md` documents the cross-language / cross-size / cross-doc-style discipline. `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/cognitive_workspace_benchmark.rs` is hermetic per the README \"Determinism\" clause. | `cognitive_workspace_benchmark` ran across all three fixtures (R70 confirmed: rust ≈4.8 ms, ts ≈2.7 ms, py ≈4.3 ms). Three fixture entries in `baselines/cognitive_workspace_metrics.json` (lines 1, 209, 422). Each fixture's `manifest.toml` declares distinct `size_class` + `documentation_style`. `golden_anchors.json` carries 8 tasks split across the three fixtures. The corpus is the spec-mandated control surface and is referenced by `metrics::regression_tests` as the canonical evidence. | **PASS.** |\n\n**Risk-controls roll-up:** every spec §Risks line has an implementation file and at least one explicit test enforcing it. Every cited test passed in this review's clean re-run.\n\n---\n\n## Verification log (R89, clean checkout, this review session)\n\n| Command | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cd daemon && cargo build --release` | **PASS.** Built in 2 m 58 s. 21 warnings, all pre-existing (R63 F-9: `identity_payload.rs` unused functions noted as a non-blocking follow-up; `mcp.rs::current_parsed_files_snapshot` unused method). Zero errors. Binary at `daemon/target/release/lattice`. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace` | **PASS.** 845 tests passed, 0 failed, 39 ignored (37 lattice-core + 1 lattice-daemon lib + 1 lattice-daemon bin). Breakdown: `lattice-core` lib `535 passed / 0 failed / 37 ignored` in 92.65 s; `lattice-daemon` lib `153 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored` in 1.33 s; `lattice-daemon` bin tests `157 passed / 0 failed / 1 ignored` in 1.61 s. Ignored tests are the `--include-ignored`-gated P99 budget tests documented in `hardening::large_repo_tests` and `consolidation::session_tests` (consistent with R88's documented `#[ignore]` pattern). |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::regression_tests` | **PASS.** 6 passed, 0 failed (the six measurable-success-criteria regression tests). |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::workspace_boundary_tests` | **PASS.** 6 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::scope_leak_tests` | **PASS.** 7 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::proposal_tests` | **PASS.** 6 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::review_queue_tests` | **PASS.** 9 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::replay_tests` | **PASS.** 6 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::scoring_tests` | **PASS.** 7 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib events::snapshot_tests` | **PASS.** 6 passed, 0 failed. |\n| `cd extension && npm run compile` | **PASS.** `tsc -p ./` clean; zero diagnostics. |\n| `cd extension && npm run lint` | **PASS.** `eslint src --ext ts` clean; zero issues. |\n| `cd extension && npm test` | **PASS.** Exit code 0 (`node ./out/test/runTest.js`). R79 confirmed the contract suite (`extension/src/test/contract.test.ts`) runs 20 tests in 495 ms